1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Most scanners give you a backlog of alerts.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Exhibit A takes a narrower position:

3
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:15,000
one finding is worth more than a wall of suspicions
when it comes with reproducible proof.

4
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:27,000
A model can raise a suspicion,
but it cannot declare a vulnerability.

5
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:36,000
Exhibit A writes an exploit and runs it
in an isolated and resource-limited sandbox.

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:42,000
It checks the oracle effect and provenance,
verifies the fix, and tests bypasses.

7
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:48,000
A green result means nothing could be proven—
not safe.

8
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:57,000
Here is a real pull request that removes containment
from a memo lookup.

9
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:07,000
The required check is red because the exploit reaches
the application entry point.

10
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:16,000
It reads the canary outside the allowed directory.

11
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:26,000
The comment shows the observed effect and provenance,
not just a pattern match.

12
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:35,000
Exhibit A proposes a small fix.
The maintainer still owns the review.

13
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:43,000
The control PR is green and does not accuse.

14
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:51,000
Prompt-injection text in a diff does not mint a finding.

15
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:58,000
A test-frame open is not application provenance.

16
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:06,000
The local dashboard is a read-only viewer of the ledger.

17
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:17,000
This is the real GitHub source:
PR runs, the proof trace, the finding,
and Economics with recorded model spend.

18
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:28,000
It does not invent a provider or budget
when the ledger did not record one.

19
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:37,000
In the live chain, fourteen PRs produced
one proven path traversal.

20
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:44,000
There were zero control accusations
and zero adversarial false proven results.

21
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:47,000
API spend was US$0.0685.

22
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:54,000
The other four vulnerable testbed PRs were green misses
because this compact run was sliced for canary_read.

23
00:02:54,000 --> 00:03:00,000
That is a documented limitation, not a safety claim.
Exhibit A: proof before accusation.
